WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.237 --> 00:00:03.390
- All right, here's a theory
I've been thinking about.

00:00:03.390 --> 00:00:06.750
Someday, maybe not next year
or five or even 10 years,

00:00:06.750 --> 00:00:09.540
but maybe someday we'll
all live in a world

00:00:09.540 --> 00:00:11.610
where we all have these wearable computers

00:00:11.610 --> 00:00:13.770
on our faces all the time.

00:00:13.770 --> 00:00:14.850
And a lot of these tech companies

00:00:14.850 --> 00:00:16.110
really believe in that future.

00:00:16.110 --> 00:00:18.000
Like I've never spoken
to anyone on Planet Earth

00:00:18.000 --> 00:00:19.890
who believes more than Mark Zuckerberg

00:00:19.890 --> 00:00:22.830
that humans are on their way to spending

00:00:22.830 --> 00:00:25.620
tons of their time in
some sort of metaverse.

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:28.440
But the tech is clearly
not good enough yet,

00:00:28.440 --> 00:00:30.660
today in 2023 for anyone to wanna do that.

00:00:30.660 --> 00:00:33.690
Like this is what a VR
headset looks like in 2023,

00:00:33.690 --> 00:00:35.100
and this is the best we've got.

00:00:35.100 --> 00:00:39.810
And even now, the computers
and pixels and batteries,

00:00:39.810 --> 00:00:42.390
and everything on your face are too much

00:00:42.390 --> 00:00:45.120
for people to wanna spend all
day in something like this.

00:00:45.120 --> 00:00:46.980
But we're all kind of on board that

00:00:46.980 --> 00:00:50.430
maybe someday the tech will
shrink down more, and more,

00:00:50.430 --> 00:00:52.590
and more and more until eventually,

00:00:52.590 --> 00:00:55.470
it's no more than just a
normal looking pair of glasses.

00:00:55.470 --> 00:00:56.940
And then maybe at that point,

00:00:56.940 --> 00:00:58.140
we'll all be cool wearing it every day.

00:00:58.140 --> 00:00:58.973
So this is Quest 3,

00:00:58.973 --> 00:01:01.470
this newest and latest and
greatest headset from Meta.

00:01:01.470 --> 00:01:04.950
My theory is, is on
this side of the scale,

00:01:04.950 --> 00:01:09.210
and on the other side of the
sliding scale is smart glasses.

00:01:09.210 --> 00:01:11.460
And meta literally is also
announcing smart glasses

00:01:11.460 --> 00:01:12.293
at their event.

00:01:12.293 --> 00:01:14.100
So these things are
literally called the RayBan

00:01:14.100 --> 00:01:17.280
Meta Smart Glasses, AKA
the RayBan Stories too.

00:01:17.280 --> 00:01:18.960
Right now, they are super simple,

00:01:18.960 --> 00:01:20.730
they don't do much
because they can only fit

00:01:20.730 --> 00:01:23.400
a camera and small
speakers, and a battery,

00:01:23.400 --> 00:01:25.080
but there are some clever tricks

00:01:25.080 --> 00:01:27.300
that enable them to do
as much as possible.

00:01:27.300 --> 00:01:30.540
And maybe someday the tech
will get powerful enough

00:01:30.540 --> 00:01:34.080
and useful enough for people
to want to use these every day.

00:01:34.080 --> 00:01:36.840
So VR headsets are racing
to get smaller and smaller,

00:01:36.840 --> 00:01:39.840
and smart glasses are racing
to get better and better tech,

00:01:39.840 --> 00:01:42.510
and they're both basically
racing towards each other,

00:01:42.510 --> 00:01:45.750
and companies like Meta are
spending tons and tons of money

00:01:45.750 --> 00:01:48.150
to develop these things to figure out

00:01:48.150 --> 00:01:50.460
which strategy will hit first.

00:01:50.460 --> 00:01:52.860
So let's see.

00:01:52.860 --> 00:01:54.210
Let's start with the headset.

00:01:54.210 --> 00:01:57.690
So this is the latest and
greatest from Meta, the Quest 3.

00:01:57.690 --> 00:02:00.330
And this is the year they made
their big pivot to it being

00:02:00.330 --> 00:02:01.950
a mixed reality headset,

00:02:01.950 --> 00:02:04.110
which in hindsight feels
like a natural progression

00:02:04.110 --> 00:02:06.330
for these things if you wanna
get them more comfortable

00:02:06.330 --> 00:02:08.760
for people to wear every day like glasses.

00:02:08.760 --> 00:02:10.560
So in previous VR headsets,

00:02:10.560 --> 00:02:12.720
it really felt like pass
through was an afterthought.

00:02:12.720 --> 00:02:14.130
Like you put the headset on,

00:02:14.130 --> 00:02:16.440
and you're just immediately
in your own world

00:02:16.440 --> 00:02:17.910
until you take the headset off.

00:02:17.910 --> 00:02:20.280
And this new version is
still built to be immersive,

00:02:20.280 --> 00:02:21.930
it still has all the light blocking

00:02:21.930 --> 00:02:23.700
and fills your field of view with screens

00:02:23.700 --> 00:02:25.260
and makes it as immersive as possible.

00:02:25.260 --> 00:02:27.870
But it now has a bunch more sensors

00:02:27.870 --> 00:02:31.020
arranged around the outside
that make pass through

00:02:31.020 --> 00:02:33.270
dramatically better than before.

00:02:33.270 --> 00:02:37.230
It's now color, stereo, very low latency,

00:02:37.230 --> 00:02:38.970
and decently high resolution.

00:02:38.970 --> 00:02:40.890
And there's immediately
a bunch of benefits

00:02:40.890 --> 00:02:43.050
to having pass through being this good.

00:02:43.050 --> 00:02:45.990
First of all, the setup
was way more intuitive.

00:02:45.990 --> 00:02:47.520
Like you can literally
take it to a new spot

00:02:47.520 --> 00:02:49.740
for the first time and
just put it on it boots up,

00:02:49.740 --> 00:02:51.300
and automatically you look down

00:02:51.300 --> 00:02:53.670
and it just maps out the
floor of the room you're in.

00:02:53.670 --> 00:02:56.070
The available floor space,
the objects in the room,

00:02:56.070 --> 00:02:57.720
the spots where you can stand,

00:02:57.720 --> 00:02:59.760
and to surprisingly great accuracy.

00:02:59.760 --> 00:03:02.100
So it's using a pair of RGB cameras

00:03:02.100 --> 00:03:04.230
and the Lidar sensor in the middle.

00:03:04.230 --> 00:03:07.620
So you no longer have to
painstakingly draw a play area

00:03:07.620 --> 00:03:08.910
every single time and stick with it.

00:03:08.910 --> 00:03:11.580
It just naturally feels
like it plants the menu

00:03:11.580 --> 00:03:13.770
floating right in the middle
of where you're standing,

00:03:13.770 --> 00:03:15.600
and you can still see
everything around you.

00:03:15.600 --> 00:03:17.670
Now you may be wondering,
okay, how good though

00:03:17.670 --> 00:03:20.100
like exactly is the Quest 3?

00:03:20.100 --> 00:03:21.360
Is it the best?

00:03:21.360 --> 00:03:23.931
Is it better than the Quest Pro?

00:03:23.931 --> 00:03:26.451
Yes, it's better than the Quest Pro

00:03:26.451 --> 00:03:29.611
but it is not as good as Apple Vision Pro.

00:03:29.611 --> 00:03:31.560
I would kind of equate it to like,

00:03:31.560 --> 00:03:33.360
if I gave you a clear pair of glasses

00:03:33.360 --> 00:03:36.630
that were not exactly your prescription.

00:03:36.630 --> 00:03:39.480
But basically this one's good
because it's stereo and color,

00:03:39.480 --> 00:03:42.270
and nearly real time, so
you see accurate colors,

00:03:42.270 --> 00:03:45.120
you look at your hands and
you can find the controllers

00:03:45.120 --> 00:03:46.050
wherever they are in the room,

00:03:46.050 --> 00:03:47.490
just pick them up and put them down

00:03:47.490 --> 00:03:49.740
without needing someone
to hand them to you.

00:03:49.740 --> 00:03:51.210
Just so many benefits like that.

00:03:51.210 --> 00:03:53.610
There's also just a small
amount of distortion

00:03:53.610 --> 00:03:54.810
with up close objects

00:03:54.810 --> 00:03:56.580
and things near the edges of your vision.

00:03:56.580 --> 00:03:59.850
But it's not quite high
enough fidelity to like

00:03:59.850 --> 00:04:02.700
pick up your phone and
start using that screen.

00:04:02.700 --> 00:04:03.930
So like if you get a text,

00:04:03.930 --> 00:04:05.310
you're still gonna have
to take the headset off

00:04:05.310 --> 00:04:06.180
to be able to read it.

00:04:06.180 --> 00:04:09.150
And I know comparing
it to a $3,500 headset

00:04:09.150 --> 00:04:11.760
feels unnecessary and it kind of is,

00:04:11.760 --> 00:04:13.380
but also a lot of people
are asking me about it,

00:04:13.380 --> 00:04:15.240
and I'm one of the few
people who can actually

00:04:15.240 --> 00:04:16.320
say they've tried both.

00:04:16.320 --> 00:04:18.990
So I will say that yes, Apple Vision Pro

00:04:18.990 --> 00:04:21.870
is still the best pass
through I've ever experienced.

00:04:21.870 --> 00:04:24.810
I distinctly remember taking
notes about my experience

00:04:24.810 --> 00:04:27.570
on my phone while still
wearing the headset,

00:04:27.570 --> 00:04:28.403
it was kind of insane.

00:04:28.403 --> 00:04:30.270
But for a $500 headset, yeah.

00:04:30.270 --> 00:04:32.130
This is absolutely as
good as you're gonna see.

00:04:32.130 --> 00:04:35.250
And combined with the high
resolution of the actual menus

00:04:35.250 --> 00:04:36.971
and the accuracy of the controllers,

00:04:36.971 --> 00:04:38.670
I think it's pretty awesome.

00:04:38.670 --> 00:04:40.320
And then of course, the
other benefit to having

00:04:40.320 --> 00:04:43.140
way higher quality sensors
around the outside of the headset

00:04:43.140 --> 00:04:45.570
is you don't actually
need the controllers.

00:04:45.570 --> 00:04:46.800
Now you've always had the choice

00:04:46.800 --> 00:04:49.770
to either use the controllers
or use your hands.

00:04:49.770 --> 00:04:51.660
And these controllers have
gotten better over the years,

00:04:51.660 --> 00:04:53.430
they're smaller, they're pretty sweet,

00:04:53.430 --> 00:04:55.350
they have better haptics than ever before.

00:04:55.350 --> 00:04:58.200
But the hand tracking has
also gotten way better

00:04:58.200 --> 00:04:59.940
and really intuitive and responsive.

00:04:59.940 --> 00:05:02.910
And I think this is key again,
to feeling like the future.

00:05:02.910 --> 00:05:06.540
So you do this pinch gesture
here to pull up the menu

00:05:06.540 --> 00:05:08.370
and move around to select things.

00:05:08.370 --> 00:05:10.170
You can literally scroll around menus

00:05:10.170 --> 00:05:12.390
by touching the digital menu

00:05:12.390 --> 00:05:14.370
and flinging them through
space with your finger.

00:05:14.370 --> 00:05:17.040
Or you can grab a window
and just move it around,

00:05:17.040 --> 00:05:18.990
putting it on a table or
floating it in the air,

00:05:18.990 --> 00:05:21.780
and it just stays locked
there, which is pretty awesome.

00:05:21.780 --> 00:05:25.650
So pretty much everything
except typing is natural.

00:05:25.650 --> 00:05:26.880
It works as you'd expect,

00:05:26.880 --> 00:05:29.250
like you're typing on a virtual
keyboard floating in space,

00:05:29.250 --> 00:05:31.050
but this will definitely
take more practice,

00:05:31.050 --> 00:05:32.760
because there's no haptic feedback.

00:05:32.760 --> 00:05:34.770
See the other gestures I was talking about

00:05:34.770 --> 00:05:36.780
almost always have a haptic feedback

00:05:36.780 --> 00:05:38.640
of your own fingers hitting each other,

00:05:38.640 --> 00:05:39.750
which is really interesting.

00:05:39.750 --> 00:05:42.480
This keyboard here,
you're sort of just poking

00:05:42.480 --> 00:05:45.450
an invisible plane in the air
where the keyboard should be,

00:05:45.450 --> 00:05:46.740
so that that's a little tougher.

00:05:46.740 --> 00:05:48.540
The main selling point
of this headset though,

00:05:48.540 --> 00:05:51.207
is still playing games, that's
still what it's super good at

00:05:51.207 --> 00:05:53.850
and it plays all the same games
that the Quest 2 could play,

00:05:53.850 --> 00:05:55.770
and there are even some
games optimized for Quest 3

00:05:55.770 --> 00:05:56.670
that it's even better at.

00:05:56.670 --> 00:05:59.850
It has this nextgen Qualcomm
Snapdragon XR2 chip,

00:05:59.850 --> 00:06:01.980
it has higher resolution per eye,

00:06:01.980 --> 00:06:04.290
it has a wider more
immersive field of view,

00:06:04.290 --> 00:06:06.270
and it's, in my opinion
slightly more comfortable,

00:06:06.270 --> 00:06:08.850
thanks to this new strap that
improves weight distribution.

00:06:08.850 --> 00:06:10.200
So I've been playing a bunch,

00:06:10.200 --> 00:06:12.450
I've really enjoyed this
golf game that feels

00:06:12.450 --> 00:06:16.080
surprisingly realistic as
someone that was expecting like

00:06:16.080 --> 00:06:18.480
wee golf levels of graphics and control.

00:06:18.480 --> 00:06:19.590
Also pinging pong,

00:06:19.590 --> 00:06:23.250
which this has this eerie
multiplayer mode online,

00:06:23.250 --> 00:06:25.860
where someone else's avatar
just shows up in your space

00:06:25.860 --> 00:06:28.544
standing 10 feet away from
you, but with no legs.

00:06:28.544 --> 00:06:32.430
But there's the classics
like Beat Saber, Super Hot,

00:06:32.430 --> 00:06:35.070
and then even some new ones
like The Rotag is Blowing Up.

00:06:35.070 --> 00:06:37.830
All this stuff is the
main reason why today,

00:06:37.830 --> 00:06:38.910
you'd buy something like this,

00:06:38.910 --> 00:06:41.280
to spend like half an hour in the thing.

00:06:41.280 --> 00:06:43.560
But again, the tech is shrinking down

00:06:43.560 --> 00:06:46.680
more and more and more,
and will every single year,

00:06:46.680 --> 00:06:50.850
until it gets close to something
like these, smart glasses.

00:06:50.850 --> 00:06:52.380
So let's talk about the smart glasses.

00:06:52.380 --> 00:06:54.300
So these are the Meta Smart Glasses,

00:06:54.300 --> 00:06:55.380
and there's others like it,

00:06:55.380 --> 00:06:57.090
but they're gonna start at
the other end of the spectrum

00:06:57.090 --> 00:06:58.830
where there's only so much stuff

00:06:58.830 --> 00:07:01.590
that you can stuff into a
regular looking pair of glasses

00:07:01.590 --> 00:07:03.715
that nobody would even look twice at.

00:07:03.715 --> 00:07:07.110
But over time, as tech gets
better and more powerful,

00:07:07.110 --> 00:07:08.430
and more miniaturized,

00:07:08.430 --> 00:07:11.160
these things will get
more and more powerful

00:07:11.160 --> 00:07:13.680
and more and more able to do more stuff.

00:07:13.680 --> 00:07:16.500
So right now this is a 12 megapixel camera

00:07:16.500 --> 00:07:19.290
with a little LED light ring
to indicate when it's recording

00:07:19.290 --> 00:07:20.670
or taking a picture.

00:07:20.670 --> 00:07:24.390
A shutter button on top, and
then a literal computer inside

00:07:24.390 --> 00:07:27.600
with some storage, a
touch pad on the side,

00:07:27.600 --> 00:07:28.710
and then some microphones,

00:07:28.710 --> 00:07:30.600
and then these really
tiny pinhole speakers

00:07:30.600 --> 00:07:33.600
that fire audio downwards
directly into your ears.

00:07:33.600 --> 00:07:34.890
It doesn't sound like much,

00:07:34.890 --> 00:07:36.930
but when paired directly to your phone,

00:07:36.930 --> 00:07:39.750
and the Meta View app, this
thing is surprisingly capable

00:07:39.750 --> 00:07:41.700
as a little computer on your face.

00:07:41.700 --> 00:07:43.500
So you can use the camera of course

00:07:43.500 --> 00:07:45.810
to just take first person
pictures and videos

00:07:45.810 --> 00:07:47.370
just by hitting the shutter button.

00:07:47.370 --> 00:07:50.250
Videos are limited to 60 seconds or less,

00:07:50.250 --> 00:07:52.020
and portrait orientation.

00:07:52.020 --> 00:07:53.040
But honestly, despite all that,

00:07:53.040 --> 00:07:55.290
they're actually pretty
solid looking videos

00:07:55.290 --> 00:07:56.490
and there's some promise here,

00:07:56.490 --> 00:07:59.340
I kind of feel like I might
want to use these for auto focus

00:07:59.340 --> 00:08:00.810
for like car driving footage,

00:08:00.810 --> 00:08:01.950
if I could get wide screen out of them,

00:08:01.950 --> 00:08:02.783
that would be awesome.

00:08:02.783 --> 00:08:03.870
And then you can also start a recording

00:08:03.870 --> 00:08:05.437
or take a picture just by saying,

00:08:05.437 --> 00:08:07.557
"Hey, Meta take a picture."

00:08:08.670 --> 00:08:10.770
And so you could see
that it was pretty fast,

00:08:10.770 --> 00:08:12.150
the little light there.

00:08:12.150 --> 00:08:13.710
I don't know if you wanna

00:08:13.710 --> 00:08:15.360
say that phrase out loud very often,

00:08:15.360 --> 00:08:16.860
so you might just stick to one of these,

00:08:16.860 --> 00:08:20.130
but yeah, it has a voice
assistant built in.

00:08:20.130 --> 00:08:21.540
So you can send and receive messages

00:08:21.540 --> 00:08:24.540
through WhatsApp Messenger,
you know, Meta stuff.

00:08:24.540 --> 00:08:26.760
But it's just audio,

00:08:26.760 --> 00:08:29.430
like there's no screen
anywhere in here built in.

00:08:29.430 --> 00:08:32.580
So this really works best with experiences

00:08:32.580 --> 00:08:35.580
that can be entirely
handled with just audio.

00:08:35.580 --> 00:08:37.590
So they're connected all
the time to your phone

00:08:37.590 --> 00:08:40.200
via Bluetooth, so you can listen to music.

00:08:40.200 --> 00:08:42.900
And these little speakers
are directional enough that

00:08:42.900 --> 00:08:45.810
at half volume, there's
really not that much bleed.

00:08:45.810 --> 00:08:48.120
And that high volume, it
kind of just sounds the same

00:08:48.120 --> 00:08:49.560
as someone like maybe
listening next to you

00:08:49.560 --> 00:08:51.617
with open back headphones.

00:08:51.617 --> 00:08:54.034
(rap music)

00:08:56.848 --> 00:08:58.410
That's as loud as it gets.

00:08:58.410 --> 00:09:02.880
But you can also ask questions of the Meta

00:09:02.880 --> 00:09:05.160
virtual assistant, little
AI virtual assistant

00:09:05.160 --> 00:09:08.370
built into the computers in
this little pair of glasses.

00:09:08.370 --> 00:09:09.307
And you have to ask it,

00:09:09.307 --> 00:09:11.400
"Hey Meta, what's the weather tomorrow?"

00:09:11.400 --> 00:09:14.143
And then it reads the answers
directly into your ears.

00:09:14.143 --> 00:09:17.340
And so now I know it's gonna rain

00:09:17.340 --> 00:09:19.170
for our last parts of the year, great.

00:09:19.170 --> 00:09:22.230
We can also ask it random
questions about people.

00:09:22.230 --> 00:09:24.480
I asked it to write a poem
and it gave me a poem.

00:09:24.480 --> 00:09:26.280
It's internet connected from your phone,

00:09:26.280 --> 00:09:27.630
so it can do a bunch of stuff.

00:09:27.630 --> 00:09:30.510
For fun, I asked it to write
an acceptance speech for me

00:09:30.510 --> 00:09:33.180
as I walk onto stage
wearing the sunglasses.

00:09:33.180 --> 00:09:34.620
And by the time I got on stage

00:09:34.620 --> 00:09:37.800
I can start saying an acceptance speech

00:09:37.800 --> 00:09:39.090
as it's reading them into my ears,

00:09:39.090 --> 00:09:41.580
which I thought was,
that's kind of a fun hack.

00:09:41.580 --> 00:09:45.720
So this is all based on Meta's
new Llama 2 language model.

00:09:45.720 --> 00:09:48.060
So it's pretty fluid and you
don't have to rely on saying

00:09:48.060 --> 00:09:50.010
certain specific phrases to get it to

00:09:50.010 --> 00:09:51.360
keep going through the conversation.

00:09:51.360 --> 00:09:53.250
Now you know, it's not
the best AI assistant

00:09:53.250 --> 00:09:55.620
I've ever heard, and it
still has its limitations,

00:09:55.620 --> 00:09:57.660
it still can't set alarms,

00:09:57.660 --> 00:10:01.301
or access third party
services that aren't Meta.

00:10:01.301 --> 00:10:05.161
But the fact that I could
be on a phone call right now

00:10:05.161 --> 00:10:09.146
and you wouldn't even notice in public,

00:10:09.146 --> 00:10:10.320
that's kind of the point.

00:10:10.320 --> 00:10:13.140
There's two different
styles by RayBan for these.

00:10:13.140 --> 00:10:16.350
These are the headliner and the Wayfarer.

00:10:16.350 --> 00:10:18.660
The downside is very clearly battery life.

00:10:18.660 --> 00:10:21.090
I mean, this is a small,
small battery to fit in here.

00:10:21.090 --> 00:10:23.310
So it's cool that you have
this wireless charging case.

00:10:23.310 --> 00:10:24.720
So the second you take them off,

00:10:24.720 --> 00:10:26.130
you can just put them in the case,

00:10:26.130 --> 00:10:28.950
and charge them back up,
just like earbuds basically.

00:10:28.950 --> 00:10:30.780
So it's more about how many times

00:10:30.780 --> 00:10:32.430
the case can charge them up.

00:10:32.430 --> 00:10:35.190
Honestly, on one charge, if
I listen to a bunch of music

00:10:35.190 --> 00:10:36.780
and take a bunch of pictures and videos,

00:10:36.780 --> 00:10:38.850
I can kill these things
in under two hours.

00:10:38.850 --> 00:10:42.510
But they're quoting 36
total hours of battery life

00:10:42.510 --> 00:10:43.680
with the charging case.

00:10:43.680 --> 00:10:45.330
By the way, the recording
light is on one side,

00:10:45.330 --> 00:10:47.220
but then it's the camera
on the other side.

00:10:47.220 --> 00:10:48.930
So that keeps it nice and symmetrical

00:10:48.930 --> 00:10:50.790
like normal glasses should be.

00:10:50.790 --> 00:10:53.970
But that's the idea, this
is about as much tech

00:10:53.970 --> 00:10:57.970
as you can fit in a normal
looking pair of glasses in 2023

00:10:57.970 --> 00:11:00.330
without it starting to look weird

00:11:00.330 --> 00:11:01.470
with the current tech we have,

00:11:01.470 --> 00:11:04.260
but it's gonna be more
and more and more stuff,

00:11:04.260 --> 00:11:06.360
and still looking like this every year.

00:11:06.360 --> 00:11:10.140
So the question is,
which side would you bet

00:11:10.140 --> 00:11:12.570
gets mass adoption first?

00:11:12.570 --> 00:11:15.360
And this is a question tech
companies have to answer

00:11:15.360 --> 00:11:16.410
before they start investing.

00:11:16.410 --> 00:11:18.270
Now Meta is invested in both.

00:11:18.270 --> 00:11:20.670
So maybe they win either
way and they're involved.

00:11:20.670 --> 00:11:23.010
But if you're Snapchat,
they've already tried,

00:11:23.010 --> 00:11:24.270
just the smart glasses,

00:11:24.270 --> 00:11:25.980
and maybe they'll keep doing that later.

00:11:25.980 --> 00:11:28.200
If you're Apple, they've
clearly started with

00:11:28.200 --> 00:11:30.960
Apple Vision Pro, and they're
gonna try to miniaturize that

00:11:30.960 --> 00:11:32.890
and shrink that year after year.

00:11:32.890 --> 00:11:34.020
But which side?

00:11:34.020 --> 00:11:36.030
And what a time to be
alive for all of this!

00:11:36.030 --> 00:11:38.400
'Cause the tech that we're
gonna have on our faces

00:11:38.400 --> 00:11:41.910
in 10, 20 years is gonna look insane

00:11:41.910 --> 00:11:43.110
compared to what we have today.

00:11:43.110 --> 00:11:45.209
The same way that the
tech we had 10 years ago

00:11:45.209 --> 00:11:48.090
looks archaic compared
to what we have now.

00:11:48.090 --> 00:11:50.130
So all that being said,
I'll leave you with this;

00:11:50.130 --> 00:11:53.460
One, Quest 3 for 500 bucks is awesome,

00:11:53.460 --> 00:11:55.080
and if you're looking to get a VR headset

00:11:55.080 --> 00:11:56.765
or a mixed reality headset at all,

00:11:56.765 --> 00:11:59.525
no problem recommending
this one, it's pretty sweet.

00:11:59.525 --> 00:12:04.110
Two, Apple's Vision Pro is still on track

00:12:04.110 --> 00:12:06.570
to be released early 2024,

00:12:06.570 --> 00:12:07.920
and I think it's gonna be pretty awesome.

00:12:07.920 --> 00:12:09.300
So make sure you get subscribed

00:12:09.300 --> 00:12:11.525
to see the review of that when it happens.

00:12:11.525 --> 00:12:15.870
And three, I'm pretty
sure we are barreling

00:12:15.870 --> 00:12:18.270
towards this computer's
on our faces future.

00:12:18.270 --> 00:12:20.280
At some point it does
feel like it's picking up

00:12:20.280 --> 00:12:22.350
that much steam and that much investment.

00:12:22.350 --> 00:12:24.090
So even if you don't believe

00:12:24.090 --> 00:12:26.040
we're all gonna be
wearing these on our faces

00:12:26.040 --> 00:12:29.100
for a super long time, it
probably won't be this,

00:12:29.100 --> 00:12:30.630
it'll be something smaller,

00:12:30.630 --> 00:12:34.200
and slowly we'll get more
and more base computer time.

00:12:34.200 --> 00:12:37.893
So which side do you pick?

00:12:39.030 --> 00:12:40.470
Thanks for watching.

00:12:40.470 --> 00:12:41.760
Catch you on the next one.

00:12:41.760 --> 00:12:43.085
Peace.

00:12:43.085 --> 00:12:45.752
